trigger: When the user types /djt-test-plan, or asks to write a manual test plan, QA steps, doer test plan, or "how do I test this change", always execute the following workflow exactly.
notes: One plan, two forms. The author runs it from an interactive artifact (links, copy buttons, result tracking). After local validation, the same plan is posted as markdown to the ticket's Doer Test Plan field. QA runs it as written. Never write a separate QA plan. Ask if the destination is unclear. Keep scope tight to the change (exclude normal regression). Only bake in target URLs you can directly observe in the repo — otherwise ask the user which environments/URLs to target before generating scripts.
